    description: "WHAT. After PR #2198 the Ruby registry is keyed by full lexical path. Left:\n- a compact declaration nested in a block whose head is a TOP-LEVEL constant (module Outer; class Inner::Thing with a top-level Inner) is keyed Outer::Inner::Thing, so Inner::Thing.run from outside is unresolved (base bound it). Grep found 5 of 2,215 nested-compact declarations in mastodon and 34 of 65,164 in gitlab; every sampled one has its head under the enclosing scope. Resolving the head needs the whole-program declared set;\n- superclass lookup inside a compactly declared scope (module A::B; class Q < X) also tries A::X, which Ruby does not;\n- extend M is treated like include M for constant lookup; a top-level include is not walked;\n- classes assigned to a constant (Struct.new, Class.new) are not symbols;\n- the core inherited-calls and inheritance linkers still identify a Ruby class by Symbol.name (chatwoot: PdfProcessingError has the correct extends edge and also a stand-in parent Base);\n- the per-file bare-method key is last-write-wins among same-named methods of one file.\nThe removal of every last-segment fallback overlaps WI-kazut. Found during PR 1 of the stable-id plan, 2026-11-15 (PR #2198). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr1/STATUS.md."  # 8894
